From 474d429ad625c1620cbc72d6231cebb7c38cb52a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: devil1993 <samanwayghatak@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 21 Aug 2026 10:30:16 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] feat(boards): edit entries in place across all five modules
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Board items (tasks, notices, lost & found, pantry, questions) were
create/delete only, so a typo or wrong date meant deleting and re-adding
— which loses the timeline (soft delete, ADR-0013) and re-notifies the
family. This adds in-place editing of author-entered content.

- Repositories: add `update(id, changes)` to every interface + both the
  Firestore and in-memory implementations, writing only content fields +
  updatedAt. No schema or Firestore-rules change — `allow update` already
  existed for soft delete.
- Hooks: each exposes an edit action with a `*_edit` telemetry event.
- UI: inline Edit -> Save/Cancel on each card (Save disabled on empty
  required text; no autoFocus, per the a11y baseline).

Editable per module: tasks (description/date), notices (text/date),
lost & found (description), pantry (name/made-on/keeps-days), questions
(text). Status/assignee/soft-delete keep their own dedicated actions.

Docs currency (ADR-0012): ADR-0018, data-model 6f-2, LikeC4 model,
in-app Guide steps, PROGRESS.md. i18n en+bn. Tests: repository update
unit test + an edit-flow test per board (94 passing).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
